{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## EXPERIMENT RESULTS (E1/E2/E3/E4) — solution VIABLE; four problems identified early\n\nOperator-authorized live+deterministic derisking complete (39 real Bedrock calls total, sonnet-4-6/haiku-4-5 tiers; raw logs+replies in session artifacts exp-e1/e2/e3 dirs).\n\n### E1 — NativeOutput x thinking on Bedrock: PARTIALLY PROVEN\n- PROVEN on the wire: outputConfig.textFormat json_schema + thinking works — sonnet-4-6 adaptive (settings thinking=True maps to type=adaptive), haiku-4-5 extended (budget_tokens=2048). No 400; the historic forced-tool_choice error does NOT occur with json_schema output; pydantic_ai auto mode selects native under thinking.\n- Bounds ge/le are STRIPPED into descriptions (model emitted 1.0 out-of-bounds) — client-side validators remain mandatory on the native path.\n- CRITICAL SCOPE FINDING: tools + thinking + native is wire-legal but the model SKIPPED the required tool 2/2 (one 306s hang); same cell with PromptedOutput called the tool with thinking intact. Layer 1 therefore applies to SINGLE-SHOT (no-tools) structured steps only; the agentic completion verifier STAYS prompted — Layer 2 is the df3a fix, not a fallback.\n- PREREQUISITE: pinned botocore 1.40.61 rejects outputConfig client-side (ParamValidationError); needs >=1.43.x.\n- Haiku needs the dated profile id us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0 (bare alias 400s at request validation).\n\n### E2 — sentinel channel, adversarial df3a shape (n=26): STRONG PASS with 2 catches\n- Sentinel compliance 16/16 (exactly one marker pair, valid JSON, true verdict every time); schema-filtered last-valid 26/26; decoy injection 0/26 (sonnet even flagged the decoy).\n- CATCH 1 (confound): the sentinel directive licenses analysis prose (quote-in-prose 0% -> 100%), which breaks today's parser 10/10 — directive and extraction MUST ship atomically, with fallback for markerless replies. The control cells' clean runs only show the current \"no prose\" directive suppressed the trigger at this n, not that today's pipeline is safe (df3a proved it is not).\n- CATCH 2 (new hazard): models fence-wrap the quoted dep record, and tolerant_parse's FENCE PRIORITY selects it even before the first-object scan — the fenced-quote path needs its own pinned regression test (covered by the design's all-fenced-blocks candidate enumeration).\n\n### E3 — selection prototype: CALLER-SAFETY PROVEN\n- 55/55 bespoke suite; df3a reproduced (3/4 layout variants fail today with \"verdict Field required\") and prototype recovers ALL 4; property test 500/500 (seed 20250804); 0.1 ms median on 100KB/32-candidate replies.\n- MECHANICAL PROOF: all 4 real pinned test files pass 110/110 with the prototype injected as parse_structured (+ injection negative-control). Zero pinned tests change; one NEW pin needed: multi-object-WITH-schema -> last-valid-wins + warning.\n- Key-overlap screen is LOAD-BEARING: without it OverlapVerdict/TicketDigest/EpicBugScreenVerdict (all-defaults contracts) degenerate to trailing junk / empty-object wins.\n- Measured residuals (accepted, not hidden): trailing-recap schema-valid decoy wins under last-wins (warning marks it; zero of five historical recurrences show that layout); candidate cap should keep the LAST 32, not the first.\n\n### E4 — schema-guided json-repair: ENGAGED\njson_repair 0.61.4 schema_from_input accepts Pydantic v2 CLASSES (richer than a schema dict — default_factory fills engage); _repair makes exactly one schema-guided call on the happy path; a missing-required-property payload raises and falls back schema-less exactly as _repair designed. The reviewer's suspicion is resolved: no silent no-op.\n\n### Net: all build-critical decisions now evidence-backed\nFix architecture stands as recorded in the previous comment, with these experiment-driven amendments: Layer 1 scoped to no-tools steps + botocore bump prerequisite + dated haiku profile id; Layer 2 ships directive+extraction atomically + pins the fenced-quote hazard; candidate-cap trims keep the last 32. Next: plan into description, review-plan, claim, implement."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785889154223003001,"uuid":"a6b78544-88a2-4d90-b257-9387f314a7de"}